This directory is the SOURCE of the platform's named images, and everything in it is derived rather than copied.

WHAT IS HERE. One `.svg` per glyph, on a 16-unit grid, named for the picture and not for the constant that wears
it (`go-left.svg`, not `NSImageNameGoLeftTemplate.svg` — three of Apple's names share one picture, and the mapping
from name to glyph is in `../../tools/system-images.py`). They are drawn as a 1.5-unit stroke with round caps and
round joins. `../../tools/system-images.py` rasterizes them at 16 and 32 pixels and writes the coverage table the
library compiles in, so THESE FILES ARE THE ART and the `.c` is the artifact.

